{"files":[{"content":"/*\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\n\n    The stencil calculation stops when (err < CONV_THRESHOLD OR iter >= ITER_MAX).\n*/\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <time.h>\n#include <sys/time.h>\n\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f // threshold of convergence\n\n// matrix to be solved\ndouble **grid;\n\n// auxiliary matrix\ndouble **new_grid;\n\n// size of each side of the grid\nint size;\nint iter_max_num;\n\n// allocate memory for the grid\nvoid allocate_memory(){\n    grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\n    new_grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\n\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\n        new_grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\n    }\n}\n\n// initialize the grid\nvoid initialize_grid(){\n    int center = size / 2;\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            // inicializa região de calor no centro do grid\n            if ( i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup){\n                grid[i][j] = 100;\n                new_grid[i][j] = 100;\n            } else {\n                grid[i][j] = 0;\n                new_grid[i][j] = 0.0;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// save the grid in a file\nvoid save_grid(){\n\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            fprintf(stdout, \"%lf \", grid[i][j]);\n        }\n        fprintf(stdout, \"\\n\");\n    }\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]){\n\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &size);\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &iter_max_num);\n\n    int hasError = 1;\n    int iter = 0;\n\n    struct timeval time_start;\n    struct timeval time_end;\n\n    // allocate memory to the grid (matrix)\n    allocate_memory();\n\n    // set grid initial conditions\n    initialize_grid();\n\n    //printf(\"Jacobi relaxation calculation: %d x %d grid\\n\", size, size);\n\n    // get the start time\n    //gettimeofday(&time_start, NULL);\n\n    while (hasError && iter < iter_max_num) {\n        hasError = 0;\n\n        // Each iteration completes its static row work and convergence\n        // reduction before the buffers are swapped for the next Jacobi step.\n        #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) reduction(|:hasError)\n        for (int i = 1; i < size - 1; i++) {\n            int row_error = 0;\n            const double * restrict current = grid[i];\n            const double * restrict above = grid[i - 1];\n            const double * restrict below = grid[i + 1];\n            double * restrict next = new_grid[i];\n\n            #pragma omp simd reduction(|:row_error)\n            for (int j = 1; j < size - 1; j++) {\n                next[j] = 0.25 * (current[j + 1] + current[j - 1] +\n                                  above[j] + below[j]);\n\n                double delta = next[j] - current[j];\n                if (delta > CONV_THRESHOLD || delta < -CONV_THRESHOLD)\n                    row_error |= 1;\n            }\n            hasError |= row_error;\n        }\n\n        double **tmp = grid;\n        grid = new_grid;\n        new_grid = tmp;\n        iter++;\n    }\n\n    // get the end time\n    //gettimeofday(&time_end, NULL);\n\n    //double exec_time = (double) (time_end.tv_sec - time_start.tv_sec) +\n    //                   (double) (time_end.tv_usec - time_start.tv_usec) / 1000000.0;\n\n    //save the final grid in file\n    save_grid();\n\n    //printf(\"\\nKernel executed in %lf seconds with %d iterations.\\n\", exec_time, iter);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/laplace_seq.c"}],"hypothesis":"Row-local restrict pointers may make the contiguous stencil accesses easier to SIMD-vectorize, while static row worksharing and a per-iteration convergence reduction preserve Jacobi dependencies. A simple completed parallel-for before each buffer swap also avoids the previous persistent-team control flow that timed out, at the possible cost of per-iteration overhead.","notes":"This is an unmeasured candidate. The stencil still reads only the previous grid, writes each interior cell once, preserves fixed boundaries, and retains the original convergence test and output formatting.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Bind each row's current, above, below, and destination data to row-local restrict pointers for the unit-stride SIMD loop.","Use static parallel row worksharing with an integer OR convergence reduction and SIMD reduction per row.","Complete each timestep's parallel-for before swapping the grid buffers and evaluating convergence again." ]}